From 62843838483293721d82cf78bb994419e31f2df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude A <claude-a@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:19:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Claude A: fix Clap/Laugh regression from B13 (wrong asset
 path + lost state machine)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TASK A22 — Final Integration Gate & Release Readiness

CODE GAP FOUND (category D — runtime/backend thuc su thieu, do B13 vo tinh
ghi de mat cong viec cua A20):

1. ui/js/audioEngine.js referenced non-existent assets/sounds/clap.mp3 and
   assets/sounds/laugh.mp3. Canonical bundled assets (Task A20, confirmed
   by Khoi) are ui/assets/sounds/Vo-Tay.MP3 (CLAP) and Cuoi-Deu.mp3
   (LAUGH). Fixed both default paths to the canonical files.

2. audioEngine.js had lost the full IDLE/PLAYING state machine that A20
   implemented and Khoi verified working (click1=play from start,
   click2=stop+reset position to 0, ended=auto-return to IDLE, loop
   always false, replay after stop/ended starts from 0). B13's version
   only exposed playClap()/playLaugh() which unconditionally restarted
   playback with no stop capability. Restored stop()/toggle()/isPlaying()/
   onChange() per-effect, fully independent between Clap and Laugh.

3. ui/js/renderer.js's clapPlayBtn/laughPlayBtn click handler was calling
   playClap()/playLaugh() unconditionally (always restart, never stop) and
   toggling the "active" CSS class blindly instead of driving it from real
   audio state. Rewired to toggleClap()/toggleLaugh() with UI state driven
   by AudioEngine.onClapChange()/onLaughChange(), so the button always
   reflects true playback state including auto-reset on ended.

4. loadData()'s knob-restore loop had dropped the Clap/Laugh volume sync
   (present in A20, lost in B13) - restored so the first play after
   restoring saved settings uses the correct volume immediately.

5. tests/unit/AudioEngine.verify.js asserted the WRONG paths as expected
   ground truth (a case of "unit test PASS masking a real bug", exactly
   what A22 warns against) - corrected assertions to canonical paths, and
   added coverage for the restored state machine (toggle/stop/onChange),
   plus a real filesystem check that the asset files actually exist.
   26 PASS / 0 FAIL (was 13/13 against the wrong behavior).

6. Removed tests/unit/ClapLaughAudio.verify.js (A20-era test extracting
   renderer.js-inline code that no longer exists after B13 moved the
   engine to its own file) - fully superseded by the corrected
   AudioEngine.verify.js above; it was throwing (not even a clean FAIL)
   since its extraction markers were gone.

VERIFIED (jsdom loading the real ui/index.html + real scripts, real click/
event dispatch, not just unit tests in isolation):
- Clap: click1 -> plays assets/sounds/Vo-Tay.MP3, loop=false, UI active=true
- Clap: click2 -> stop, currentTime=0, UI active=false
- Clap: simulated ended -> auto IDLE, currentTime=0, no click needed
- Laugh: click1 -> plays assets/sounds/Cuoi-Deu.mp3, independent of Clap

NOT TOUCHED: ManualPriorityGuard, AI_CONTROL/ControlSource, Key/Mod/BPM
engines, Beat/Master separation (BEAT_INPUT_VOLUME/MASTER_OUTPUT_VOLUME
still fully independent, unaffected), MIDI/DAW mapping architecture,
ui/index.html (no HTML changes - script tag for audioEngine.js already
existed from B13).
